      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-10-07_WidnesExaminer_art0162" n="art0162">
        <head>KING AND QUEEN'S LAST GAME</head>
        <p>KING AND QUEEN'S LAST GAME</p>
        <p>President's Main Nl'inner Gets "Clean-Plated." • • The King and 'Queen Club brought their season to a close on Saturday with a successful main. The final game was won by W. Holloway, who defeated G. Clifford by 15-10. The surprise of the day was the defeat in the first round of W. Johnstone, winner of the President's main, E. Balmer not allowing him to score. The following are the details of the play : First Round. J: Craddock S. Leigh W. Chadwick S. Green J. Watkins E. Rowlands H. Wilde G. Jones E. Balmer T. Carter J. Warburton R. Savory G. Clifford .......... 15 I. Kaye H. Oatley J. Moorfield W. Holloway ....... 15 F. Clare Second Round. J. Warburton G. Jones ...... :..... 15 S. Green .... J. Watkins W. Chadwick G. Clifford E. Rowlands ........ 15 H. Wilde 7 R. Savory W. Holloway 15 J. Craddock Third Round. G. Clifford G. Jones E. Rowlands W. Holloway Semi-Final. W. Holloway . l5 E. Rowlands ....... 11 G. Clifford Final. W. Holloway</p>
      </div>
