        <p>road, has received a letter from her son stating, that he is wounded. The letter, dated Septem- ber 30th, ran as follows :—" I got wounded in two places, the right thigh and the left calf and with a bit of luck I shall be in England this time next week." Corporal Mannion, who is 21 years of age, had been in the Army two years, and at the Front 19 months. He was educated at St. Mary's School and was formerly employed as a moulder by • Messrs. Fletcher, Russell and Co., Ltd. He was an enthusiastic Rugby foot- ball player, having taken part in many of the Works' Competitions and also having played with the Latchford Rangers' team. PRIVATE F. LIOLLINGSWORTIL -- Wounded Just Above Ankle Of The Right Leg. Private Frank Hollingsworth, Royal Innis- killing Fusiliers, and son of Mrs. Hollings- worth, 157, Knutsford-road, is officially reported</p>
