        <p>PRIVATE T. O'DAY. Wounded.</p>
        <p>PRIVATE WILLIAM TITCRARD. - A Willing Lad And Good Soldier Suffers Prom Shell Shock. Private William Titchard, South Lancashire Regiment, son of Mr. and Mrs. Thomas Titchard, 16, Birchalf-etreet, has been wounded in France, whither he proceeded with the South Lancashires sixteen months ago. Lance Corporal Wood, one of his chums, writing "to break the news" to his parents, says :—" Your</p>
