        <p>• • BO WLING-• CALEDONIAN ASSOCIATION v. LIBERAL CLUB. The retum match between teams representing the above was played on the Cemetery Bowling Green last Saturday. The Liberal Clilb won by 52 (singles) and 16 (doubles), or 68 in all. After the match the teams had tea at the hotel, Mrs. Denham catering in very acceptable manner. Mr. William Murray, president of the Caledonian Asso- ciation, presided, and said it was always a plea- sure to meet the Liberal 'Club bowlers, if the 4 could not beat them; they would keep on trying. Alderman Tinnion, replying, said it was a plea- sure to meet the Caledonians, who were all good sports. He also referred to the fact that the local Scotsmen had done good work for the 'various charities. On the motion of Councillor J. T. Locker, Mr. and Mrs. Denham were thanked for the catering; and Messrs. A. E. Clayton and G. Marshall were thanked for conducting the match. Scores :- Caledonians. Liberal Club. W. Murray (capt.) 9 Ald. Tinnion(capt.) 2 G. Thomson ..... 5 13 Coun. J. T. Locker 9 5 H. Hope ..... 1 T. O'Brien P. H. Brown .... 4 7 W. Boyle W. Mitchell ...-... 9 J. Gibson J. Robertson J. McDermid J. Buchanan J. Fleming A. G. Allen J. Bennett H. Bell J. Tennant W. Stirling Jos. Foster G. Ball R. W. Antwis ... 9 W. Daintith ..... 5 G. Marshall ...:.. 1 13 J. Pollitt G. Allen - Lester ' 92 79 144 95 • BANK QUAY CHARITY MAIN. The abovb main was completed on Saturday, the final being won by A. Gleave, sen., who accounted, for J. Daintith, 13-10. The following were the winners :- 1, All. Gleave, sen. (scr.) 13-10; 2, J. Daintith (8.Q.) (3) 13-8; B. 'Jennings (3) 13-10; 4, John Appleton (scr.) 13-6; 5, J. Thomas. jun. (3) 13-10; 6, J. Harrison (1) 13-12; 7, W. Massey (2) 13-10; 8, A. Broadhurst (scr.) 13-12; 9, G. Savage (4) 13-7; 10, C. Hocigkins (4) 13-12; 11, J. Pritchard (5) 13-7; 12, J. Daintith (H.) (4) 13-11; 13, A. Middleton (3) 13-12; 14, C. Smith (4) 13-8; 15, W. Whatmough (3) 13-11; 16, J. Watson (3) 13-9. Other winners in last 64 :-H. Webster (5) 13-12; :F. Cadclick (4) 13-9; R. Warburton (3) 13-12;J. Brown (5) walk-over; R. Jefferson (2) 13-6; T. Moore (4) 13-11: J. Bettley (5) 13-12: H. Orsburne (4) 13-9; W. Saunders (5) 13-5; J. Hands (3) 13-9: T. Jackson (4) 13-9; G. Willcox. jun. (2) 13-12; John Gleave (owes 1) 13-9; G. Willcox, sen. (4) 13-7; J. Barratt (4) 13-11; J. Watts (3) 13-5. CONSERVATIVE MAIN. Sixty-four entries were received for the final main of the Senior Conservative Club, held on Saturday. Some fine games were witnessed, and in the final T. Cooper (1) secured a popular victory over F. Holland (5) by 13-12. Sixty wounded soldiers were entertained to tea by the members during the afternoon. The following were the winners :- First Round.-H. P. Turner (1), F. Holland (5), A. Broady (scr.), S. Hewitt (4), T. Webb (4), D. Bibby (5), P. Bradburn (4), W. Pritchard (4), A. Ellison (2), B. Jolley (4), T. Cooper (1), R. Straw (1), C. Woods (3), S. Wray (3), A. Mather (4), E. Jones (3), T. Horrabin (1), E. Gleave (1), J. Gorst (5), J. Mottram• (5), W. Millington (1), T. Weir (3), T. Hill (4), T. Hackett (1). G. Warburton (1), B. J. Dendy (4) and H. Mather (3). A. Scott (1), B. 'Fairhurst (6), J. Lodge (1), J. Corradine (4) and J. H. Gittens (1) walked over. Second Round.-R. Straw, E. Gledve, T. Horra- bin. T. Webb, B. Jolley, F. Holland, A. Mather, A. Billiton, W. Pritchard, B. J. Dendy, T. Cooper, S. Hewitt, A. Broady, H. Mather, E. Jones and W. Millington. Third Round.-T. Cooper, B. Jolley, A. Broady, W. Millington, F. Holland, R. Straw, B. J. Dendy and S. Hewitt. Fourth Round. A. Broady F. Holland B. Jolley, T. Cooper Semi-Final. T. Cooper F. Holland T. Cooper (1)</p>
